# Trivy findings ignored by id, each with its reason and the condition that
# removes it. Same rule as auditConfig.ignoreGhsas in pnpm-workspace.yaml: one
# id, never a severity threshold or a package.

# CVE-2026-85024 (medium) — undici's WebSocket permessage-deflate cleanup drops
# the inflate stream's error listener, so a peer that sends a payload past the
# 128 MiB limit followed by a malformed DEFLATE byte crashes the process. Fixed
# in 7.29.1. It reached the vulnerability database on 2026-09-28 or 29, which is
# why this check began failing every pull request at once.
#
# The vulnerable copy is 7.29.0, and every miniflare release pins
# `undici: 7.29.0` exactly, including the latest (5.20260926.0-alpha), so no
# upgrade reaches the fix. An override would hand miniflare a version it never
# declared, the trade pnpm-workspace.yaml refuses for sharp in the same place.
#
# Exposure: undici arrives through miniflare (the wrangler dev server and
# @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers) and jsdom (the admin tests). Trivy counts it
# as a production dependency only because @sentry/cloudflare names wrangler as an
# optional peer. A Worker never bundles undici — Workers use the runtime's own
# fetch and WebSocket — and nothing in the dev server or the tests opens a
# WebSocket to an untrusted peer.
#
# Remove this entry when miniflare pins undici 7.29.1 or later. The expiry makes
# the check fail again on that date, so it is re-checked rather than forgotten.
CVE-2026-85024 exp:2026-12-31

# CVE-2026-93687 (GHSA-vfj7-8cjw-p6xm, high) — braces' brace-pattern parser can
# be driven into exponential backtracking by a crafted pattern, so a malicious
# glob string spins the process. Exposure is dev-only OpenAPI tooling:
# @stoplight/prism-cli and @stoplight/spectral-cli reach braces through
# postman-collection, and no patched release exists to move to. The waiver is by
# id because Trivy reports this advisory under its CVE.
#
# Reason: dev-only OpenAPI tooling with no patched release to override to.
# Removal condition: Remove this entry when a fixed braces release is published
# and the OpenAPI tooling accepts it. The expiry (2026-11-05) makes the check
# fail again on that date, so it is re-checked rather than forgotten.
CVE-2026-93687 exp:2026-11-05

# GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w (high) — sharp's bundled libvips decodes a crafted image
# with an out-of-bounds write. Exposure is dev-only through miniflare (the
# wrangler dev server and @cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers); no parent release
# ships sharp >=0.35.5 yet, and sharp's native platform packages are not
# exercised by the tests. This advisory has no CVE id, so Trivy is silenced by
# GHSA id.
#
# Reason: dev-only through miniflare, with no parent release shipping
# sharp >=0.35.5 yet.
# Removal condition: Remove this entry when a miniflare release ships
# sharp >=0.35.5. The expiry (2026-11-05) makes the check fail again on that
# date, so it is re-checked rather than forgotten.
GHSA-wq5f-xc86-pv6w exp:2026-11-05
